.TH VEIL 1 "July 2025" "VeilOS 0.6" "VeilOS User Manuals"
.SH NAME
veil \- the interactive shell for the VeilOS AI-native operating system
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B veil
.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBveil\fP program is the primary user interface for VeilOS. Unlike traditional shells, it does not interpret commands based on a rigid parser. Instead, it accepts natural language input, which is processed through a cognitive loop to determine user intent.
.P
The shell's primary function is to act as a conversational partner, allowing the user to direct the operating system by stating high-level goals rather than specific, technical commands.
.SH INTERACTION MODEL
Interaction with \fBveil\fP is based on a continuous dialogue.
.TP
.B 1. User Input
The user provides a prompt in plain English.
.TP
.B 2. Logic Chain
The system analyzes the input and presents a "Logic Chain," which is a brief summary of the interpreted intent and the plan it has formed to address it. This provides transparency and allows the user to understand the system's reasoning before it acts.
.TP
.B 3. Execution
The system executes the plan, which may involve running background tasks, interacting with the filesystem, or making further AI queries.
.TP
.B 4. Response
The system provides a final response in natural language, confirming the completion of the task.
.SH EXITING
To exit the shell, type \fBexit\fP or press Ctrl+C.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wsm (7),
.BR mcp (7)
